   230	## 8. 30/60/90 roadmap
   231	
   232	### Days 1–30 — Establish the foundation
   233	
   234	- Inventory all 16 enabled conversion actions and assign each to Consulting, Physiotherapy or another scope.
   235	- Create the approved Consulting conversion-goal hierarchy.
   236	- Demote newsletters and soft actions; exclude Physiotherapy actions from Consulting goals.
   237	- Confirm CRM, click-ID capture, call qualification and offline-upload design.
   238	- Complete Australian privacy/legal review, CMP and consent design.
   239	- Build and QA the dedicated landing-page variants and two-step form.
   240	- Extend the resolved Search evidence with longer-history query and keyword-performance pulls; audit the 493 negatives; pull RSAs, assets, settings, Quality Score components and geo/device reports.
   241	- Repair the existing Brand ad group, remove all three confirmed duplicates from the five service groups, and verify routing and separated metrics before considering breakout.
   242	- Prepare one isolated Meta prospecting build but keep it unpublished.
   243	- Keep PMax and paid remarketing parked.
   244	
   245	**Committed leading indicators:** approved goal map; zero newsletter primaries; test-event reconciliation; privacy approval; LP/form QA passed; at least 30 days of search terms reviewed.
   246	
   247	### Days 31–60 — Launch controlled tests
   248	
   249	- Route approved Search themes to their relevant landing-page variants.
   250	- Retain Maximize Conversions while the clean baseline forms.
   251	- Launch one consolidated Meta website-lead prospecting ad set under Scenario 1 or 2.
   252	- Fund Meta at no less than A$20/day.
   253	- Use at least three materially distinct formats and five approved creatives.
   254	- Optimise initially to valid Snapshot requests; each Snapshot placement must state: **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
   255	- Validate click-ID, UTM, CRM-stage, Pixel/CAPI and deduplication flows.
   256	- Build Consulting-only retargeting audiences without activating a separately underfunded ad set.
   257	- Review search terms weekly and classify any product or Physiotherapy bleed.
   258	
   259	**Committed leading indicators:** approved destination coverage; minimum Meta delivery floor; delivery, CTR, form-start and Snapshot-request baselines; identifiers retained; no known cross-business bleed left unclassified.
   260	
   261	### Days 61–90 — Diagnose and decide
   262	
   263	- Assign each Search cluster a status: retain, repair, insufficient data or candidate test.
   264	- Compare Meta concepts and formats without fragmenting the budget.
   265	- Replace the provisional Meta CPA assumption with observed Snapshot-request data.
   266	- Reconcile raw leads to CRM-qualified leads and proposals.
   267	- Complete the commercial target-CPA worksheet or mark it not assessable.
   268	- Issue a written PMax fund-to-floor or park decision.
   269	- Issue a separate paid-remarketing rebuild or park decision.
   270	- Propose any budget increase in increments no greater than 20%, followed by 3–5 days of observation and conversion-lag review.
   271	
   272	No segment receives an unconditional kill or scale label during the first 90 days. The 3× Kill Rule requires an approved clean target CPA, and the methodology’s full scaling threshold of at least 50 conversions per week is far above the current approximately 20 real leads per month.
   273	
   274	Any 12-month lead, CPA or revenue trajectory remains an assumption-labelled scenario—not a commitment.
