   186	- Capture GCLID, GBRAID, WBRAID, FBCLID and UTMs in the CRM.
   187	- Send qualified-lead, proposal and closed-won outcomes through Google Data Manager and Meta CAPI.
   188	- Implement server-side GTM on a first-party domain such as `tags.ergoworksconsulting.com.au`.
   189	- Use a Conversion Linker and Meta Pixel plus CAPI, preferably through CAPI Gateway.
   190	- Use matching browser/server `event_id` values for deduplication.
   191	- Use Data-Driven Attribution where eligible; do not use rule-based attribution.
   192	- Implement **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, through an approved CMP.
   193	- Enforce no pre-consent advertising or analytics transmissions unless Australian privacy/legal review explicitly approves a different configuration.
   194	- Keep Consulting separate from Physiotherapy, ErgoEquip and Biosymm through dedicated or tightly scoped GA4 stream, Meta Dataset/Pixel, GTM triggers, audiences and CRM mappings.
   195	
   196	### First-90-day measurement commitments
   197	
   198	- 100% of approved Primary actions documented and tested.
   199	- Newsletter and soft actions removed from Consulting bidding goals.
   200	- Physiotherapy actions excluded from campaign 700072710 goals.
   201	- CRM lead IDs and event IDs captured on valid lead records.
   202	- Offline-event latency below 24 hours where operationally possible; 24–72 hours is a warning range.
   203	- Meta lead-event EMQ of at least 8.0.
   204	- Browser/server deduplication of at least 90%.
   205	- Server/client hit ratio between 80% and 120%.
   206	- At least six applicable Meta match parameters on eligible events.
   207	- Weekly platform-to-CRM reconciliation.
   208	- Zero sensitive-data events or parameters detected in testing.
   209	
   210	The primary commercial KPI is **cost per qualified lead (CPQL)**. Raw CPL remains an entry-stage diagnostic. CAC and target CPQL cannot be set until contract value, contribution margin and stage-conversion rates are verified.
   211	
   212	The full event taxonomy, consent requirements, field allowlist/deny list and QA plan are in [Appendix C](./appendices/C-tracking-spec.md).
   213	
   214	### Methodology conflict
   215	
   216	The generic ads-budget rubric recommends Maximize Clicks below 30 conversions per month. The live campaign, however, is mature, already uses Maximize Conversions and generates approximately 20 real leads per month while its current conversion signal is polluted.
   217	
   218	Automatically switching to Maximize Clicks during measurement repair could optimise for traffic volume before query quality is understood. The account-specific recommendation is therefore to retain Maximize Conversions while cleaning and restabilising the baseline, then reassess:
   219	
   220	| Clean post-remediation condition | Bidding decision |
   221	|---|---|
   222	| Fewer than 20 clean conversions/month with weak delivery and no qualified-lead imports | Consider a controlled Maximize Clicks test only after query review and with an evidence-based CPC cap |
   223	| Approximately 20–29 clean conversions/month with stable query and lead quality | Retain Maximize Conversions and document the rubric variance |
   224	| At least 30 clean conversions/month with stable CPA | Maximize Conversions is supported; assess tCPA readiness |
   225	| More than 50 clean conversions/month with stable qualified-lead CPA | Consider tCPA |
   226	| Reliable margin values and sufficient closed-won volume | Assess tROAS |
   227	
   228	Do not use ECPC.
   229	
   230	## 8. 30/60/90 roadmap
   231	
   232	### Days 1–30 — Establish the foundation
   233	
   234	- Inventory all 16 enabled conversion actions and assign each to Consulting, Physiotherapy or another scope.
   235	- Create the approved Consulting conversion-goal hierarchy.
   236	- Demote newsletters and soft actions; exclude Physiotherapy actions from Consulting goals.
   237	- Confirm CRM, click-ID capture, call qualification and offline-upload design.
   238	- Complete Australian privacy/legal review, CMP and consent design.
   239	- Build and QA the dedicated landing-page variants and two-step form.
   240	- Extend the resolved Search evidence with longer-history query and keyword-performance pulls; audit the 493 negatives; pull RSAs, assets, settings, Quality Score components and geo/device reports.
   241	- Repair the existing Brand ad group, remove all three confirmed duplicates from the five service groups, and verify routing and separated metrics before considering breakout.
   242	- Prepare one isolated Meta prospecting build but keep it unpublished.
   243	- Keep PMax and paid remarketing parked.
   244	
   245	**Committed leading indicators:** approved goal map; zero newsletter primaries; test-event reconciliation; privacy approval; LP/form QA passed; at least 30 days of search terms reviewed.
   246	
   247	### Days 31–60 — Launch controlled tests
   248	
   249	- Route approved Search themes to their relevant landing-page variants.
   250	- Retain Maximize Conversions while the clean baseline forms.
   251	- Launch one consolidated Meta website-lead prospecting ad set under Scenario 1 or 2.
   252	- Fund Meta at no less than A$20/day.
   253	- Use at least three materially distinct formats and five approved creatives.
   254	- Optimise initially to valid Snapshot requests; each Snapshot placement must state: **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
   255	- Validate click-ID, UTM, CRM-stage, Pixel/CAPI and deduplication flows.
   256	- Build Consulting-only retargeting audiences without activating a separately underfunded ad set.
   257	- Review search terms weekly and classify any product or Physiotherapy bleed.
   258	
   259	**Committed leading indicators:** approved destination coverage; minimum Meta delivery floor; delivery, CTR, form-start and Snapshot-request baselines; identifiers retained; no known cross-business bleed left unclassified.
   260	
   261	### Days 61–90 — Diagnose and decide
   262	
   263	- Assign each Search cluster a status: retain, repair, insufficient data or candidate test.
   264	- Compare Meta concepts and formats without fragmenting the budget.
   265	- Replace the provisional Meta CPA assumption with observed Snapshot-request data.
   266	- Reconcile raw leads to CRM-qualified leads and proposals.
   267	- Complete the commercial target-CPA worksheet or mark it not assessable.
   268	- Issue a written PMax fund-to-floor or park decision.
   269	- Issue a separate paid-remarketing rebuild or park decision.
   270	- Propose any budget increase in increments no greater than 20%, followed by 3–5 days of observation and conversion-lag review.
   271	
   272	No segment receives an unconditional kill or scale label during the first 90 days. The 3× Kill Rule requires an approved clean target CPA, and the methodology’s full scaling threshold of at least 50 conversions per week is far above the current approximately 20 real leads per month.
   273	
   274	Any 12-month lead, CPA or revenue trajectory remains an assumption-labelled scenario—not a commitment.
   275	
   276	## 9. Risks and compliance gates
   277	
   278	| Gate | Requirement | Launch consequence |
   279	|---|---|---|
   280	| Claims | No guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance, quantified claims reduction or guaranteed financial outcome | Blocks affected creative or page copy |
   281	| Snapshot description | Every placement must state: preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis | Blocks affected ad, form or page |
   282	| OAIC APP 3 | No injury, symptom, diagnosis, treatment, claim or other health fields in advertising forms | Blocks form launch |
   283	| Meta personal attributes | Use workplace- and role-level language; never imply that the viewer or their team has a health condition | Blocks affected Meta creative |
   284	| Consent | Required enquiry consent must be separate from optional, unchecked marketing consent | Blocks form launch |
   285	| Privacy | Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent. CMP, pixel/CAPI field mapping, call tracking and CRM uploads require Australian privacy/legal approval | Blocks all new paid-social, LP tracking, remarketing and offline activation |
   286	| Sensitive data | No free-text enquiry content, medical data, call content or Physiotherapy data may be sent to advertising platforms—even hashed | Blocks measurement activation |
   287	| Proof | Awards, “ASX 100,” 5.0/63 reviews, client logos and Danone references are **client sign-off required** wherever proposed | Blocks those proof assets |
   288	| Isolation | Campaign-level controls and Consulting-specific measurement scope must prevent ErgoEquip, Biosymm and Physiotherapy contamination | Blocks affected campaign or dataset |
   289	| PMax | Clean goals, offline loop, dedicated LP, verified assets, URL controls, exclusions and A$50/day funding | Otherwise remains parked |
   290	| Remarketing | Privacy approval, sufficient isolated audiences, approved creative, frequency controls and separate viable funding | Otherwise remains parked |
   291	
   292	This document authorises planning only. It does not authorise live-account, website, CRM or tracking changes.
   293	
   294	## 10. Open decisions
   295	
   296	The decisions Marcus and the client need to resolve are summarised below and detailed in [Open Questions](./open-questions.md):
   297	
   298	- Is Meta’s A$600 minimum added on top of Search or reallocated from it?
   299	- Can PMax receive its full A$50/day floor without destabilising Search?
   300	- What average contract value, delivery margin and close rate define the allowable CAC and target CPQL?
   301	- Which CRM will hold click IDs, consent and lead-stage outcomes?
   302	- How far should Consulting and Physiotherapy be separated across Ads, GA4, GTM and Meta?
   303	- Should PMax and paid remarketing be funded properly or remain parked?
   304	- How many Snapshot requests can the team deliver and follow up?
   305	- Which reviews, logos, awards and client references are substantiated and approved?
   306	- Who owns landing-page development and where will it be hosted?
   307	- What future subdomain or route should host the private shareable campaign page?
   308	
   309	## Not assessed / data required before implementation
   310	
   311	| Area | Data or decision required | What it enables |
   312	|---|---|---|
   313	| Search queries and competitor/generic-group terms | Last 90 days plus trailing 12 months; the last-30-day pull is resolved | Longer-history query-quality diagnosis and evidence-based controls |
   314	| Keyword and negative history | Trailing-12-month keyword performance plus audit of the resolved 493-negative inventory | Structure, routing, overblocking and overlap decisions |
   315	| RSAs, assets and Quality Score components | Current and recent creative history; expected CTR, ad relevance and landing-page experience | Relevance, eligibility and landing-page diagnosis |
   316	| Geography, devices and campaign settings | Geo/device performance plus location targets, presence, networks and other complete settings | Leakage, presence, device and network decisions |
   317	| Brand post-repair evidence | Query demand, impression share, lost share and auction insights after in-place consolidation | Retain repaired ad group versus campaign breakout |
   318	| Conversion configuration | All 16 enabled actions and campaign-specific goal mappings | Clean Consulting bidding objective |
   319	| Call outcomes | Duration plus business-purpose dispositions | Qualified-call validation |
   320	| CRM pipeline | Qualified, proposal, won, revenue and contribution-margin stages joined to click IDs | Target CPQL, CAC and value-bidding readiness |
   321	| PMax history and controls | Assets, search categories, themes, URLs, exclusions, goals and historical outcomes | Fund-to-floor versus park decision |
   322	| Remarketing configuration | Audience sources, size, duration, exclusions, frequency and history | Rebuild versus park decision |
   323	| Privacy and consent | CMP, collection notices, vendor flows, retention and legal approval | Pre-launch approval |
   324	| Proof permissions | Substantiation and written approval for reviews, logos, awards, Danone and “ASX 100” | Paid-media proof usage |
   325	| Commercial economics | Average contract value, delivery margin, close rates and acceptable payback | Real target CPA and conditional kill/scale thresholds |
   326	| Delivery capacity | Snapshot volume, response time and follow-up ownership | Safe Meta pacing and lead handling |

