81:## Proposed budget scenarios
85:The scenarios are anchored to both the approximately **A$40,000 trailing-12-month Search investment** and the observed **A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range**, using the verified last-30-day spend of **A$4,246** as the exact planning baseline.
87:For Meta planning, the initial optimisation event is website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only—not raw Search enquiries or soft actions. No observed Meta lead-entry CPA exists; the provisional range below is derived from the lower-friction Snapshot path and remains assumption-based:
89:- **Assumption 1:** a Snapshot Request costs **25%–40%** of the A$212.30 Search raw-enquiry CPL because it is a free, lower-friction lead magnet.
90:- **Assumption 2:** A$212.30 × 25%–40% produces a provisional Snapshot-request CPA range of **A$53.08–A$84.92**.
91:- **Planning anchor:** use the conservative upper end, **A$84.92 per Snapshot Request**, until Meta produces clean observed data.
92:- **Upper-bound sensitivity only:** A$212.30 remains a conservative raw-enquiry-CPL sensitivity; it is not the Meta target-CPA anchor.
93:- The commercial target remains not assessable pending average contract value, contribution margin and qualified-lead rate.
95:### Scenario 1 — Current-budget reallocation; PMax parked
97:This scenario holds total media at the verified last-30-day spend. Meta receives its delivery floor, so the resulting mix cannot reach 70/20/10.
99:| Channel | Calculation | Proposed 30-day budget | Actual share |
101:| Google Search | A$4,246 − A$600 | **A$3,646** | **85.87%** |
102:| Meta | A$20/day × 30 | **A$600** | **14.13%** |
103:| PMax plus remarketing | Parked | **A$0** | **0.00%** |
104:| **Total** |  | **A$4,246** | **100.00%** |
106:Decision: use only if the budget must remain flat. Meta’s A$600 budget passes both the delivery floor and the provisional A$424.60 learning-budget check for one ad set. Treat this as a controlled baseline-establishment test because the Snapshot-request CPA is assumption-based and commercial lead economics remain unknown.
108:The A$600 must sit in **one consolidated prospecting ad set**. A separately funded remarketing ad set would push each ad set below the A$20/day floor; therefore, build remarketing audiences during this scenario but park paid retargeting until volume and budget support it.
110:### Scenario 2 — Minimum-viable Meta added on top
112:This scenario protects the existing Search run-rate and adds the Meta delivery floor, which is higher than the provisional learning-budget requirement.
114:| Channel | Calculation | Proposed 30-day budget | Actual share |
116:| Google Search | Existing last-30-day baseline | **A$4,246.00** | **87.62%** |
117:| Meta | Higher of A$600 delivery floor and 5 × A$84.92 | **A$600.00** | **12.38%** |
118:| PMax plus remarketing | Parked | **A$0.00** | **0.00%** |
119:| **Total** |  | **A$4,846.00** | **100.00%** |
121:Decision: preferred minimum launch scenario. It protects the existing Search run-rate while funding one Meta ad set above both sufficiency checks. It does not achieve the intended 80/20 active-channel mix; that overlay should not override the current event-level planning assumptions or platform floor.
123:Meta receives **A$20/day** over 30 days. Keep this in one consolidated prospecting ad set initially. Build retargeting audiences but do not fragment the budget.
125:### Scenario 3 — Minimum-viable Meta plus PMax at its floor
127:This scenario keeps the existing Search baseline, adds minimum-viable Meta and funds PMax at A$50/day.
129:| Channel | Calculation | Proposed 30-day budget | Actual share |
131:| Google Search | Existing last-30-day baseline | **A$4,246.00** | **66.91%** |
132:| Meta | Higher of A$600 delivery floor and 5 × A$84.92 | **A$600.00** | **9.45%** |
133:| PMax | A$50/day × 30 | **A$1,500.00** | **23.64%** |
134:| Display remarketing | Parked initially | **A$0.00** | **0.00%** |
135:| **Total** |  | **A$6,346.00** | **100.00%** |
137:Decision: use only after the measurement and landing-page gates pass. Platform floors materially override 70/20/10: PMax becomes 23.64% rather than 10%, while Search is 66.91% and Meta is 9.45%.
139:Do not divide the A$1,500 testing budget between PMax and Display remarketing. PMax alone consumes the testing floor. Remarketing remains parked until its audience size, incremental role and separate budget are established.
141:### Platform sufficiency checks
143:| Check | Formula | Result | Status |
145:| Meta delivery floor | A$20/day × 30 | A$600 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Scenarios 1–3 pass with one ad set |
146:| Raw Search enquiry CPL | A$4,246 last-30-day Search spend ÷ approximately 20 real leads | A$212.30 | Conservative upper-bound sensitivity only—not the Meta target-CPA anchor |
147:| Assumed Snapshot-request CPA range | A$212.30 × assumed 25%–40% lower-friction-event factor | A$53.08–A$84.92 | Assumption-based pending clean Meta Snapshot-request data |
148:| Provisional Meta target CPA | Conservative upper end of assumed Snapshot-request CPA range | A$84.92 | Planning anchor only—not a qualified-lead or profitable-acquisition target |
149:| Meta learning budget | 5 × A$84.92 | A$424.60 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Scenarios 1–3 pass with one ad set; A$600 delivery floor is controlling |
150:| Raw-enquiry-CPL upper-bound sensitivity | 5 × A$212.30 | A$1,061.50 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Sensitivity only; not used to set the proposed Meta budgets |
151:| PMax floor | A$50/day × 30 | A$1,500 per 30-day planning period | Only Scenario 3 passes |
152:| PMax under a 10% slice at current spend | 10% × A$4,246 | A$424.60 per 30-day planning period, or A$14.15/day | Fails the A$50/day floor by A$1,075.40 per 30-day planning period |
153:| Total budget needed for PMax to equal exactly 10% | A$1,500 ÷ 10% | A$15,000 per 30-day planning period | Well above the observed A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range |
155:The A$84.92 figure is an assumption-labeled event-level planning anchor, not a commercially defensible target CPA. The A$212.30 raw-enquiry CPL is retained only as an upper-bound sensitivity. A further caveat on the derivation: the "approximately 20 real leads" denominator is undifferentiated and may include certificate-intent conversions — "manual handling certificate" alone drew 55 clicks / 1.67 conversions in the last 30 days (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`) and those conversions are unclassified as individual versus organisational — so both A$212.30 and the derived A$84.92 anchor could be understated as costs per genuine corporate lead. Average contract value, contribution margin, qualified-lead rate, close rate and service capacity are unknown. Until those inputs and a clean conversion baseline exist:
157:- do not apply target CPA bidding;
158:- do not make unconditional pause or scale decisions;
159:- assess provisional Meta learning sufficiency against website `Lead`, while labelling A$84.92 as a Snapshot-path planning assumption rather than a blended observed CPA;
160:- replace the assumed range with observed Snapshot-request CPA as soon as clean Meta data is available;
161:- replace the planning anchor with a qualified-lead and contribution-margin-based ceiling as soon as CRM data is available.
