321:| `ergonomic assessment sydney` | 100 | 0 | **A$6.00** | Commercial geo intent; Geo group and dedicated assessment landing-page variant |
322:| `ergonomic assessment perth` | 100 | — | A$1.80 | Geo group, but publication blocked pending service-coverage sign-off |
323:| `ergonomic assessment canberra` | 30 | — | — | Geo group, but publication blocked pending service-coverage sign-off |
324:| `online ergonomic workstation assessment` | 90 | — | — | Remote group; organisational WFH/workstation framing |
325:| `online ergonomic assessment` | 60 | — | — | Remote group; organisational framing and query review |
327:Sydney and Melbourne are high-value but pricey assessment terms. Their A$6.00/A$7.00 Ahrefs CPC estimates justify tight Exact/Phrase structure and close search-term review, not an unconditional manual bid or scale instruction. Pair them with the dedicated assessment landing-page variant and qualified-lead measurement before any budget increase. All scale and bid-strategy changes remain conditional on a clean conversion baseline (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §5).
329:Canberra is not a Keyword Planner hypothesis: `ergonomic office canberra` (EXACT, QS=3) and `ergonomic office fyshwick` (PHRASE, ENABLED, QS=5) already exist as live keywords, and the fyshwick term produced **3 conversions from A$250.00 / 18 clicks at 26% CTR** in the last 30 days — observed converting inventory. Gate: Fyshwick is Canberra's furniture-retail district, so the query may carry equipment/showroom intent; pull the ad and conversion type behind that term before building on it, and treat any Canberra recommendation as conditional on the clean-conversion baseline (3 conversions is thin).
331:Additional commercial modifiers such as `corporate`, `workplace`, `for employees`, `onsite` and `Australia` remain proposed hypotheses. The city and near-me volumes in the coverage sheet are Ahrefs-verified; they need service-coverage approval and Google geo-performance evidence, not volume re-verification, before publication or bid modification.
