348:### Proposed campaign-level negative themes
350:A large negative inventory already exists: **419 campaign-level plus 74 ad-group-level negatives on campaign 700072710** (`research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`). The task is therefore not building a list from scratch but **auditing the existing 493 negatives** for overblocking, staleness (many single-name/person negatives suggest long accumulation) and gaps around the confirmed waste terms (certificate-intent and regulator queries from the 2026-07-12 search-terms pull).
352:New candidates must be validated against actual Search Terms Reports. Use Exact negatives for specific irrelevant searches and Phrase negatives for clearly irrelevant intent patterns. Do not use speculative broad-match negatives.
356:| Theme | Proposed candidates | Control |
358:| DIY/informational | `"diy"`, `"assignment"`, `"essay"`, `"student"`, `"university"`, `"tafe"`, specific irrelevant free-template or definition queries | Avoid excluding `training`, `course`, `checklist`, `assessment tool` or `free` categorically without query evidence because they may overlap legitimate services or the approved offer |
359:| Jobs | `"jobs"`, `"job vacancy"`, `"career"`, `"salary"`, `"resume"` | Campaign-level Consulting negatives |
360:| ErgoEquip product bleed | `"buy ergonomic chair"`, `"officeworks"`, `"ikea"`, `"bunnings"`, `"standing desk for sale"`, specific chair/desk/keyboard/mouse/monitor-arm/footrest shopping queries | Do not block generic ergonomic equipment language without confirming commercial-service irrelevance |
361:| Physiotherapy de-mix | `"physiotherapist"`, `"physio near me"`, specific treatment/clinic/appointment queries | Campaign-level only; never account-wide because the shared account includes an active Physiotherapy campaign |
362:| Consumer/medical | Specific patient-treatment, diagnosis or symptom-treatment queries found in the report | Do not broadly exclude terms such as `pain` until actual queries and conversion paths are reviewed |
363:| CPR / first-aid bundle — conditional | `"cpr"` only if ErgoWorks confirms it does not deliver or partner on CPR; retain/review the existing `"first aid"` PHRASE and `[first aid and manual handling training]` EXACT controls rather than duplicating them | Ahrefs shows bundled demand at 150/month for `manual handling and cpr training` and 70/month for `manual handling and first aid training`, but keyword research is not a Search Terms Report. Hold any new negative until service scope is confirmed and an actual irrelevant query validates the match type |
364:| Vehicle ergonomics | `[driver ergonomic assessment]` if an actual irrelevant query appears; no duplicate additions for car/vehicle terms | The legacy list already has `car` BROAD, `[car ergonomic assessment]` EXACT and `[vehicle ergonomic assessment]` EXACT. Audit the over-broad `car` control and retain or narrow the exact controls; Ahrefs identifies car/vehicle/driver tails at 40/40/30 searches/month as out of scope |
365:| Assessment software / SaaS | `[ergonomic assessment software]` as the narrow candidate after Search Terms Report confirmation | The verified term has 40 searches/month and SaaS intent. Existing controls include `app` BROAD and several software-specific negatives, but not this exact phrase; audit the broad controls for overblocking and do not run this term as a positive ErgoAssess keyword |
366:| Free manual-handling variants | No duplicate addition while `free` BROAD remains live; after the audit, replace or retain only evidence-backed Exact/Phrase controls such as `[manual handling course free]` and specific `"free online"` query patterns | The campaign already has `free` BROAD and `[manual handling course free]` EXACT. Because Broad negatives can overblock and the approved Snapshot itself uses “free,” audit routing and duplication before any change; source any replacement from actual irrelevant Search Terms Report queries |
367:| Regulator/government informational | `"work safe australia"`, `"safe work"`, `"safework"`, `"workforce australia"`, `"high risk work licence"` as Exact/Phrase negatives at campaign level | These are non-commercial government-lookup queries matched into the DSA/generic groups with 0 conversions ("work safe australia" A$84.53 / 2 clicks / 0 conv). Note: a `worksafe` BROAD negative already exists in the 419-list — audit for duplication first, and verify the DSA-group leakage is a match-type/exact-competitor-keyword gap rather than a missing negative |
368:| Existing 493-negative audit | Full audit of the existing 419 campaign-level + 74 ad-group-level negatives | Review for (a) blockers against the approved care-sector, online, refresher and certificate trial sets, including `"aged care"`, `disability`, healthcare variants, `[online manual handling course]` and `[manual handling refresher course]`; (b) overblocking from generic single-token Broad negatives such as `certification`, `courses`, `advice`, `free`, `car` and `app`; (c) redundancy with the candidate themes above; and (d) stale person/name negatives — approximately 40+ individual first-name BROAD negatives (e.g. `adam`, `carol`, `emma`) — reviewed for retention versus removal |
370:#### Certificate-intent decision table
372:“Manual handling certificate” is the largest single search term by spend in the **2026-07-12 30-day top-60 pull** (A$364.86 / 55 clicks / 1.67 conv ≈ 3% CVR, versus “manual handling training” at ~13.6%), but certificate queries are not uniformly waste: “manual handling certificate online australia” produced **1.33 conversions from A$15.92**. The buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED** in current conversion data.
376:| Verified certificate/course term | AU vol/mo | KD | Approx. Ahrefs CPC (planning A$) | Planning implication |
378:| `manual handling certificate` | **2,800** | 39 | A$1.00 | Commercial + transactional demand head; buyer type unclassified |
379:| `manual handling course` | **600** | 30 | A$1.00 | Part of the same certificate/course parent-topic pool; buyer type unclassified |
380:| `manual handling certificate online` | **150** | 43 | A$1.30 | Mixed online/certificate intent; Search-only and organisational qualification required |
381:| `accredited manual handling training` | **60** | 37 | A$0.90 | Makes accreditation a keyword-visible question; never imply accreditation without client evidence and sign-off |
383:The certificate + course head alone is approximately **3,400 searches/month**, with another 210/month across the verified online-certificate and accredited terms before close-variant overlap. This strengthens Option A because it tests a material pool, but volume does not classify the buyer as organisational. Do not blanket-exclude. Use these complementary controls as evidence permits:
385:| Option | Mechanics | Trade-off |
387:| **A — dedicated Certificate / Course mixed-intent split (RECOMMENDED, gated trial)** | Build as `GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3`, Search-only, using Exact + Phrase and organisational qualification; route to the Manual Handling variant's certificate block. Do not build or publish until the client confirms whether ErgoWorks issues an accredited certificate, statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records | The verified approximately 3,400+ search/month pool makes the trial material rather than fringe, but buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED**. **Gated on the LP certificate block, accreditation and participant-record evidence, and client sign-off** (Appendix A); excluded from Meta |
388:| **B — exact-negative individual phrasings (can coexist with A)** | Exact negatives only on clearly individual searches such as personal-validity, personal-card or individual-accreditation phrasings; rely on the existing #1 organic blog ranking for excluded individual demand | Blocks only the exact clearly individual queries selected; it does not block broader corporate/online certificate queries unless those exact converting phrases are added in error |
390:“Accredited manual handling training” at **60 searches/month** makes accreditation a keyword-visible product question. ErgoWorks must confirm whether it provides accredited training, a statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records before the term, claim or landing-page block can publish; absent that evidence, do not bid on accreditation intent and do not imply equivalence. In either option, **Meta never targets certificate intent** (see Appendix D).
