468:### Meta budget and learning design
470:| Scenario | Meta budget | Proposed structure | Sufficiency |
472:| Scenario 1 | A$600 per 30 days; A$20/day | One prospecting ad set | Passes A$600 delivery floor and provisional A$424.60 learning check |
473:| Scenario 2 | A$600 per 30 days; A$20/day | One prospecting ad set | Passes delivery and provisional learning checks while preserving the Search baseline |
474:| Scenario 3 | A$600 per 30 days; A$20/day | One prospecting ad set | Passes delivery and provisional learning checks; PMax separately receives A$1,500 |
476:The **provisional** learning check is **5 × A$84.92 = A$424.60** per ad set, based on the assumption-labeled Snapshot-request CPA anchor. It is not independently assessable until a real post-cleanup CPA exists. The independent **A$20/day delivery floor = A$600 per 30 days** is the only verified sufficiency check and therefore the controlling minimum.
478:Do not split A$600 across interests, broad, lookalike and retargeting ad sets. Each additional ad set would independently require at least A$20/day and at least 5× its event-level target CPA for learning.
480:Future scaling note (not launch): if the Meta budget later increases under the 20%-increment rule (Scenarios 2–3 trajectory), a geo-weighted or ACT-specific ad set may be considered — but only once volume supports a second ad set independently meeting the A$600 per 30 days / A$20 per day floor. The Canberra pocket is real but small (3 conversions); do not fragment the single consolidated ad set now.
482:### Meta launch-quality requirements
484:- At least five creatives in the launch ad set.
485:- At least three materially different formats where Appendix D production permits.
486:- Creative concepts must differ in angle, format, visual treatment, hook and headline—not merely minor variants.
487:- Target a pre-launch creative-diversity score of at least 8/10 under the concept, format, visual, hook and headline rubric.
488:- Keep video at no more than 15 seconds for Stories/Reels and no more than 30 seconds for Feed.
489:- Keep headlines under 40 characters and primary text under 125 characters where practical.
490:- Review creative fatigue every 14 days; a CTR decline greater than 20% is a diagnosis flag, subject to sufficient delivery.
491:- Aim for prospecting seven-day frequency below 3.0.
492:- The free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot must be B2B-only, limited in scope and accompanied by: **“Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.”**
493:- Do not use awards, Danone, logos, “ASX 100” or 5.0/63 reviews unless marked and cleared as **client sign-off required** before publication.
