   370	#### Certificate-intent decision table
   371	
   372	“Manual handling certificate” is the largest single search term by spend in the **2026-07-12 30-day top-60 pull** (A$364.86 / 55 clicks / 1.67 conv ≈ 3% CVR, versus “manual handling training” at ~13.6%), but certificate queries are not uniformly waste: “manual handling certificate online australia” produced **1.33 conversions from A$15.92**. The buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED** in current conversion data.
   373	
   374	Ahrefs now verifies that this is a large demand pool rather than a fringe tail (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §2). The CPC figures below are approximate Ahrefs planning inputs, **not observed Google Ads CPC**:
   375	
   376	| Verified certificate/course term | AU vol/mo | KD | Approx. Ahrefs CPC (planning A$) | Planning implication |
   377	|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
   378	| `manual handling certificate` | **2,800** | 39 | A$1.00 | Commercial + transactional demand head; buyer type unclassified |
   379	| `manual handling course` | **600** | 30 | A$1.00 | Part of the same certificate/course parent-topic pool; buyer type unclassified |
   380	| `manual handling certificate online` | **150** | 43 | A$1.30 | Mixed online/certificate intent; Search-only and organisational qualification required |
   381	| `accredited manual handling training` | **60** | 37 | A$0.90 | Makes accreditation a keyword-visible question; never imply accreditation without client evidence and sign-off |
   382	
   383	The certificate + course head alone is approximately **3,400 searches/month**, with another 210/month across the verified online-certificate and accredited terms before close-variant overlap. This strengthens Option A because it tests a material pool, but volume does not classify the buyer as organisational. Do not blanket-exclude. Use these complementary controls as evidence permits:
   384	
   385	| Option | Mechanics | Trade-off |
   386	|---|---|---|
   387	| **A — dedicated Certificate / Course mixed-intent split (RECOMMENDED, gated trial)** | Build as `GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3`, Search-only, using Exact + Phrase and organisational qualification; route to the Manual Handling variant's certificate block. Do not build or publish until the client confirms whether ErgoWorks issues an accredited certificate, statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records | The verified approximately 3,400+ search/month pool makes the trial material rather than fringe, but buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED**. **Gated on the LP certificate block, accreditation and participant-record evidence, and client sign-off** (Appendix A); excluded from Meta |
   388	| **B — exact-negative individual phrasings (can coexist with A)** | Exact negatives only on clearly individual searches such as personal-validity, personal-card or individual-accreditation phrasings; rely on the existing #1 organic blog ranking for excluded individual demand | Blocks only the exact clearly individual queries selected; it does not block broader corporate/online certificate queries unless those exact converting phrases are added in error |
   389	
   390	“Accredited manual handling training” at **60 searches/month** makes accreditation a keyword-visible product question. ErgoWorks must confirm whether it provides accredited training, a statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records before the term, claim or landing-page block can publish; absent that evidence, do not bid on accreditation intent and do not imply equivalence. In either option, **Meta never targets certificate intent** (see Appendix D).
