--- A headings / key terms ---
1:# Appendix A — Landing Page Wireframe + Full Copy
3:## Purpose and conversion objective
5:Build one dedicated, long-form landing-page system on `ergoworksconsulting.com.au`, with three message-matched variants:
11:These pages replace the generic WordPress destinations currently receiving paid traffic. The business case for the dedicated LP rests on **message match, offer and form — not speed**: the live site is already fast (Lighthouse 97 mobile on the manual-handling page, LCP 2.0s, CLS 0, per `research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md` §Lighthouse), so the new page must merely not regress below those thresholds. The system supports the existing mature Google Search program—approximately **A$40,000 trailing 12 months**, with an observed range of **A$3.0k–A$4.7k per month** and approximately **20 real leads per month**—and the proposed Meta demand-generation activity.
13:The commercial objective is **cost per qualified lead**, progressing to cost per held consultation and pipeline generated. Newsletter sign-ups, unqualified form completions and other soft actions are not success metrics.
15:The launch-default dominant CTA is the **free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot** for organisations. It covers one defined workplace question and provides a written three-point summary. **It is preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.** Service-plan-primary variants are post-baseline tests only.
17:## Modular wireframe
19:All three variants use the same modular page structure. Only the hero, benefit emphasis, process language, proof selection, FAQs and form defaults change.
21:| Order | Module | Purpose | Required execution |
23:| 1 | Stripped header | Establish legitimacy without creating exits | ErgoWorks logo, “Australia-wide workplace ergonomics” — **client sign-off required (see geography launch blocker)**, optional clickable phone number and one primary CTA. No full navigation, service dropdowns, store links or physiotherapy links. |
24:| 2 | Hero | Confirm ad relevance immediately | Exact service phrase in the H1, outcome-led subhead, one dominant CTA, short qualification line and relevant workplace image. |
25:| 3 | Proof strip | Reduce initial uncertainty | Maximum three verified signals. Every proposed proof asset remains marked **client sign-off required** until substantiated and approved. |
26:| 4 | Benefit blocks | Explain controllable business outputs | Three concise blocks covering visibility, prioritisation and implementation—not guaranteed health, injury, compliance or claims outcomes. |
27:| 5 | How it works | Make delivery concrete | Three or four steps with clear inputs, activities and buyer deliverables. |
28:| 6 | Snapshot offer | Provide a low-commitment next step | State scope, recipient, output and limitation. Always display: **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.** |
29:| 7 | Service detail | Support buyers who need more evidence | Variant-specific delivery formats, likely outputs and suitable organisational use cases. |
30:| 8 | Proof section | Answer vendor-risk objections | Consultant credentials, approved examples, sample deliverables and testimonials only after verification and permission. |
31:| 9 | FAQ | Resolve commercial and operational objections | Cover scope, locations, delivery format, equipment independence, privacy and the limits of the Snapshot. |
32:| 10 | Final CTA and form | Convert evidence-seeking visitors | Repeat the same dominant CTA, embed the two-step form and show what happens next. |
33:| 11 | Minimal footer | Provide necessary legal and contact information | Privacy policy, terms, business contact details and consent-management link. No cross-sell to ErgoEquip or Biosymm. |
35:### Page-level rules
37:- One page variant per intent cluster; do not present training, assessment, software, physiotherapy and equipment as competing actions.
38:- Use the exact service phrase from the ad in the H1 and naturally within the first screen.
39:- Match the ad’s CTA to the landing-page CTA. Target the skill’s **100% message-match standard**: headline, offer and CTA aligned.
40:- Keep the Snapshot visibly B2B: use “organisation”, “workplace”, “WHS”, “HR”, “Facilities” and “team-size band”.
41:- Keep the clickable phone number secondary to the form CTA.
42:- Do not link to ErgoEquip or Biosymm. Consulting analytics, pixels, GA4 stream and GTM scope must remain isolated from those businesses and from Physiotherapy activity in the shared Ads account.
43:- Avoid health or injury narratives, personal-attribute messaging and open text boxes that invite medical information.
44:- Do not claim that the service guarantees injury prevention, ensures WHS compliance, eliminates absenteeism or produces a stated reduction in claims.
45:- Use only controllable promises: defined scope, task review, practical training, documented observations, prioritised actions, manager guidance and implementation tracking.
46:- Show a CMP without covering the headline, CTA or form. Consent controls must not delay form interaction by more than one second.
47:- AU privacy review, CMP and consent implementation are pre-launch gates.
48:- **All LP variants ship `noindex,follow` with a canonical to the closest existing service page.** Organic is negligible for this domain (15 keywords, ~60 visits/month), so there is no SEO upside — and indexing the LP risks cannibalising the one organic asset that matters: a blog post ranking **#1 for "manual handling certificate"** (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md` §Ahrefs). The LP must not chase SEO; index only if the client later retires that blog post.
49:- **Geography claim is a LAUNCH BLOCKER, not a passive sign-off item.** The live site commits to Sydney and Melbourne only, while this appendix's header/proof strip says "Australia-wide … client sign-off required" and search terms span Canberra, Sydney, Brisbane and national terms. The only converting geo-specific term is `ergonomic office fyshwick` (the Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane/near-me geo terms appear in the pull but did not convert). The LP cannot claim broader coverage than the live site until verified; if coverage IS Sydney/Melbourne-only, the Canberra spend needs a geo decision, not just copy (see open-questions.md, service-geography question).
53:## Variant 1 — Manual Handling Training
55:### Hero
61:# Make manual handling training specific to the work being performed
63:ErgoWorks helps WHS, HR and operational teams connect practical training with the manual tasks, work patterns and control priorities present in their workplace. **Delivery format and service scope are client-sign-off required; do not publish onsite or online capability until confirmed.**
65:*Research supports testing online intent, but it does not verify delivery capability. Hold any online claim behind client sign-off and keep any approved framing organisational (“for your team”)—never an individual e-learning promise.*
69:**Get a free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot**
71:*For one defined workplace question, with a written three-point summary. Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.*
82:### Certificate disqualifier / reframe block (new module, directly after the hero)
84:“Manual handling certificate” is the largest single search term by spend in the **2026-07-12 30-day top-60 pull** (**A$364.86 / 55 clicks / 1.67 conversions**, per `research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`), yet the live page never says “certificate” once. Some certificate queries convert (“manual handling certificate online australia” produced 1.33 conversions from A$15.92), but buyer type is unclassified — treat this as mixed individual/corporate intent until CRM classification confirms it. This is therefore a disqualifier-plus-reframe block on this variant — not a separate page and not silence.
86:## Looking for a manual handling certificate?
88:Proposed copy, **client sign-off required:** “ErgoWorks delivers **workplace group training with participant attendance or training-completion records for organisations**. It does not issue individual accredited certificates.” Neither statement may be published as fact until the client verifies it. No “nationally recognised” or RTO claim may appear unless separately verified.
90:- **Individuals** seeking a personal certificate: politely route out (link to suitable external information or the existing blog article; no form push).
91:- **Corporate certificate-seekers** (“we need our staff certified”): route into the same Snapshot/scope CTA using client-approved participant attendance/training-completion-record framing.
93:*Snapshot CTA here carries the standard adjacent limitation: preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.*
