99:- Australia-wide delivery — **client sign-off required**
100:- Named consultant qualifications and professional memberships — **client sign-off required**
101:- Approved training or manual-task client example — **client sign-off required**
103:### Benefit blocks
105:## Training connected to real workplace tasks
111:## Practical priorities for workers and managers
115:**Buyer receives:** tailored learning content and supporting materials; participant attendance or training-completion records are **client sign-off required** and must not be promised until verified.
117:## A pathway beyond the session
123:### Scope-pending modules — do not publish before client sign-off
125:These modules are production placeholders, not current capability claims. Publish only the modules the client confirms, using the approved onsite/remote geography and delivery scope.
127:#### Care-sector team training — gated
129:For aged-care, healthcare or disability-support organisations planning workplace training for teams and supervisors. **Do not publish until sector scope is confirmed, the live aged-care/disability/healthcare negatives are reconciled, and onsite/remote geography is approved.** Never imply that the viewer or a participant has a disability, injury or health condition.
131:#### Online team delivery — gated
133:For organisations seeking a delivery format for distributed or hybrid teams. **Client sign-off required on whether online delivery is supported, for which programmes, and in which geography.** Do not promise individual e-learning or credential outcomes.
135:#### Refresher pathway — gated
137:For organisations reviewing whether team training should be refreshed or connected to an ongoing programme. **Client sign-off required on refresher capability, cadence, participant outputs and geography.** Do not imply a mandated frequency.
139:### How it works
141:## From workplace need to practical delivery
143:### 1. Define the tasks and audience
147:### 2. Scope the programme
149:Agree on delivery format, session length, site requirements, content boundaries and any task-observation inputs.
151:### 3. Deliver practical training
153:After delivery-format and service-scope sign-off, run the agreed programme using examples relevant to the work being performed. **Do not publish onsite or virtual capability until confirmed.**
155:### 4. Document next steps
157:Provide supporting materials and any scoped observations or priority actions. Attendance records are **client sign-off required** and must not be promised until verified.
159:*The exact inclusions, delivery format and turnaround must be confirmed in the proposal.*
161:### Canonical offer registry — client approval required before launch
163:| Stage | Offer | Eligibility / best fit | Exact deliverable and pricing status | Required caveat |
165:| Entry | **Free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot** | B2B organisational buyer with one defined workplace-ergonomics question; capacity and service geography must be approved | 15-minute consultant conversation and written three-point summary; free, subject to approved fulfilment capacity | Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis |
166:| Paid entry | **ErgoStart** | Defined site, cohort or issue | Fixed-scope assessment sprint and prioritised actions; pricing unconfirmed and must not be advertised until client-approved | Scope, inclusions, delivery timing and price are confirmed only in an approved proposal |
167:| Rollout | **ErgoScale** | Corporate, multi-site or hybrid programme | Repeatable workflow, implementation plan and reporting; pricing unconfirmed | Coverage, timing and outputs depend on the approved programme scope |
168:| Capability | **ErgoCoach** | Manual-task or train-the-trainer need | Task-led review, tailored training and supervisor toolkit; pricing unconfirmed | Format, participants and outputs depend on the approved scope |
169:| Ongoing | **ErgoControl** | Organisation requiring ongoing programme visibility | ErgoAssess subscription or managed retainer, review cadence and reporting; pricing unconfirmed | Platform, service level, cadence and outputs depend on the approved scope |
171:The Snapshot gives cold prospects a concrete next step without asking them to commit immediately to a full programme. The offer names, eligibility, fulfilment promise and ladder remain **client sign-off required**.
