943:## Testing order and decision rules
947:1. Dedicated message-matched page versus current generic destination. The control is not a slow page: it is a fast (Lighthouse 97), content-heavy but conversion-weak page — single "Make an Enquiry" CTA, full navigation with 30+ links, zero certificate handling and a keyword-stuffed body. Name the specific hypotheses the live page hands us so the test is interpretable rather than "new vs old": **stripped nav vs 30+ nav links; Snapshot offer vs bare enquiry form; certificate block vs none.**
948:2. Snapshot CTA versus service-specific scope CTA
952:6. Proof beside hero CTA versus proof after “How it works”
953:7. Optional phone field versus no phone field
955:9. Two-step form versus a shorter single-step control, only after a clean baseline exists
957:Judge tests on qualified-lead and held-conversation outcomes where sample size permits. Raw form-fill improvements are insufficient if qualification rate deteriorates.
959:No absolute pause, kill or scale directive should be applied until the target CPA, qualified-lead definition and clean conversion baseline are approved. Any broader 3× kill or 20% scale rule remains conditional on those inputs and sufficient comparable data.
