   828	## Mobile and performance requirements
   829	
   830	The skill benchmark indicates that mobile can represent more than 75% of ad clicks and reports an 82.9% cross-industry mobile share. These are planning benchmarks, not verified ErgoWorks device data.
   831	
   832	### Mobile layout
   833	
   834	- Keep the H1, core benefit, CTA and Snapshot limitation visible in the first screen where practical.
   835	- Use a full-width primary CTA.
   836	- Use a sticky CTA only after the visitor scrolls past the hero; it must not obscure content or consent controls.
   837	- Keep tap targets at least **48 × 48 px**, with at least **8 px** spacing.
   838	- Use body text of at least **16 px**.
   839	- Use the correct mobile keyboard for email and phone inputs.
   840	- Keep the phone number clickable with a `tel:` link.
   841	- Avoid horizontal scrolling, carousels and auto-playing audio.
   842	- Do not show an interstitial or popup on arrival.
   843	- Keep form labels visible; do not rely on placeholders as labels.
   844	- Place proof close to the CTA rather than below an excessively long service explanation.
   845	- Ensure the CMP can be dismissed without scrolling and does not cover the CTA.
   846	
   847	### Performance acceptance criteria
   848	
   849	| Metric | Pass | Warning | Fail |
   850	|---|---:|---:|---:|
   851	| Largest Contentful Paint | Under 2.5s | 2.5–4.0s | Over 4.0s |
   852	| Interaction to Next Paint | Under 200ms | 200–500ms | Over 500ms |
   853	| Cumulative Layout Shift | Under 0.1 | 0.1–0.25 | Over 0.25 |
   854	| Time to Interactive | Under 3.0s | 3.0–5.0s | Over 5.0s |
   855	| Page weight | Under 2MB | 2–5MB | Over 5MB |
   856	
   857	Implementation guidance:
   858	
   859	- Use responsive WebP or AVIF hero assets, ideally under 200KB.
   860	- Preload only critical fonts and avoid unnecessary font weights.
   861	- Lazy-load below-fold images.
   862	- Minimise third-party scripts, chat tools and heatmaps.
   863	- Prevent the form, proof strip and consent banner from causing layout shifts.
   864	- QA on representative mobile devices and network conditions before traffic is switched.
   865	
   866	These thresholds are build acceptance criteria only, not a sales argument: the existing pages were technically assessed on 2026-07-12 and are fast (live manual-handling page Lighthouse 97 mobile, LCP 2.0s, CLS 0; homepage 98/1.6s). One additional acceptance line applies: **the new LP must match or beat the live page's LCP of 2.0s.** This is a real risk, not a formality — marcuscaporaso.com/ergoworks/campaign-plan scored 92 with LCP 3.3s, so a new LP on a similar stack could be slower than the page it replaces.
   867	
   868	---
   869	
   870	## Measurement and attribution requirements
   871	
   872	### Event design
   873	
   874	| Funnel stage | Canonical event | Source of truth | Google bidding treatment | Meta bidding treatment |
   875	|---|---|---|---|---|
   876	| Snapshot request | `snapshot_request` | CRM-confirmed form submission | Initial Primary | Initial website `Lead` optimisation event |
   877	| Direct enquiry | `direct_enquiry` | CRM-confirmed form submission | Initial Primary | Initial website `Lead` optimisation event |
   878	| Call connected | `call_connected` | Call-tracking platform | Secondary | Reporting only |
   879	| Qualified call | `qualified_call` | CRM/call disposition applying W-Audit rule | Primary only via qualified import once reliable | Send through CAPI; optimisation only after reliable volume |
   880	| Qualified lead | `lead_qualified` | CRM stage | Secondary while validated; future Primary | Future `QualifiedLead`/conversion-leads optimisation signal |
   880	| Qualified lead | `lead_qualified` | CRM stage | Secondary while validated; future Primary | Future `QualifiedLead`/conversion-leads optimisation signal |
   881	| Proposal | `proposal_sent` | CRM stage | Secondary | CAPI reporting/custom audience |
   882	| Won | `closed_won` | CRM finance-approved stage | Value-bearing secondary initially | CAPI value event and audience exclusion |
   883	
   884	Newsletter sign-up, email click, page view and form start must not be primary bidding conversions.
   885	
   886	Additionally, capture a `variant_intent` hidden-field value for certificate-block engagement (e.g. block viewed/clicked) as a **secondary signal only — never a bidding conversion** — so the certificate disqualifier's deflection-versus-capture rate is measurable before deciding on negatives for the ~A$364/30-day "manual handling certificate" term.
   887	
   888	Snapshot booked and held are CRM stages only, not platform events.
   889	
   890	Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only.
   891	
   892	### Attribution data
   893	
   894	Capture and pass through to the CRM:
   895	
   896	- `gclid`
   897	- `gbraid` and `wbraid` where applicable
   898	- `fbclid`
   899	- Meta `_fbc` and `_fbp`
   900	- UTM source, medium, campaign, content and term
   901	- Landing-page variant
   902	- Form version
   903	- Referring URL
   904	- First-touch and latest-touch timestamps
   905	- Consent status and notice version
   906	
   907	Preserve click IDs across form steps and redirects. Do not place sensitive employee or health information in URLs, data-layer objects or advertising events.
   908	
   909	### Platform implementation
   910	
   911	- Retain Google Ads auto-tagging.
   912	- De-mix Consulting and Physiotherapy conversions within Ads account `9258098368`.
   913	- Keep ErgoWorks Consulting tags and data isolated from ErgoEquip and Biosymm.
   914	- Use a dedicated ErgoWorks Consulting pixel/GA4 stream/GTM scope.
   915	- Configure Meta Pixel and CAPI with matching `event_name` and `event_id`.
   916	- Target Meta event deduplication of at least **90%** and EMQ of at least **8.0** as set by the broader plan.
   917	- Use enhanced conversions for leads and offline/CRM outcome import.
   918	- Use DDA; do not use deprecated rule-based attribution.
   919	- Implement a CMP and **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, subject to AU privacy review.
   920	- Verify that enquiry and marketing consent are stored separately.
   921	- Fire `snapshot_request` or `direct_enquiry` once only, according to the submitted form path and after successful server acceptance—not on button click or Step 1 completion.
   922	- Confirm that the thank-you state cannot be refreshed to create duplicate conversions.
   923	
   924	### Reporting
   925	
   926	Report by page variant, source, campaign, ad group, search theme and lead stage:
   927	
   928	- Landing-page sessions
   929	- Form-start rate
   930	- Step 1-to-Step 2 continuation
   931	- Form-completion rate
   932	- Qualified-lead rate
   933	- Snapshot booking and held rate
   934	- Cost per submitted lead
   935	- Cost per qualified lead
   936	- Cost per held conversation
   937	- Proposal and won pipeline, when available
   938	
   939	The skill’s broad landing-page and professional-services conversion benchmarks are directional only. They are not Australia-specific or ergonomic-consulting-specific and must not become committed ErgoWorks targets.
   940	
   941	---
   942	
   943	## Testing order and decision rules
   944	
   945	Run tests sequentially where traffic is limited:
   946	
   947	1. Dedicated message-matched page versus current generic destination. The control is not a slow page: it is a fast (Lighthouse 97), content-heavy but conversion-weak page — single "Make an Enquiry" CTA, full navigation with 30+ links, zero certificate handling and a keyword-stuffed body. Name the specific hypotheses the live page hands us so the test is interpretable rather than "new vs old": **stripped nav vs 30+ nav links; Snapshot offer vs bare enquiry form; certificate block vs none.**
   948	2. Snapshot CTA versus service-specific scope CTA
   949	3. Manual Handling hero copy option
   950	4. Workstation / Assessment hero copy option
   951	5. Hybrid / Home-office hero copy option
   952	6. Proof beside hero CTA versus proof after “How it works”
   953	7. Optional phone field versus no phone field
   954	8. Calendar offered after submission versus consultant follow-up
   955	9. Two-step form versus a shorter single-step control, only after a clean baseline exists
   956	
   957	Judge tests on qualified-lead and held-conversation outcomes where sample size permits. Raw form-fill improvements are insufficient if qualification rate deteriorates.
   958	
   959	No absolute pause, kill or scale directive should be applied until the target CPA, qualified-lead definition and clean conversion baseline are approved. Any broader 3× kill or 20% scale rule remains conditional on those inputs and sufficient comparable data.
   960	
   961	---
   962	
   963	## Pre-launch acceptance checklist
   964	
   965	- The ad, H1, offer and CTA match exactly.
   966	- Only one dominant CTA appears throughout each variant.
   967	- The Snapshot limitation appears every time the offer is presented.
   968	- No copy guarantees injury prevention, compliance, claims reduction or medical outcomes.
   969	- No copy implies that the viewer or an employee has a health condition.
   970	- No form field requests injury, symptom, diagnosis or medical information.
   971	- Enquiry acknowledgement and optional marketing consent are separate.
   972	- All proof is verified, permissioned and approved.
   973	- No ErgoEquip, Biosymm or Physiotherapy link, tag, audience or conversion contaminates the page.
   974	- AU privacy review is complete.
   975	- CMP and consent behaviour are approved and tested.
   976	- Mobile tap, font, form and banner requirements pass.
   977	- Performance thresholds pass.
   978	- Click IDs and UTMs reach the CRM.
   979	- Pixel/CAPI events deduplicate correctly.
   980	- `snapshot_request` or `direct_enquiry` fires once after successful submission.
   981	- CRM stages support qualified-lead feedback.
   982	- Thank-you state and optional calendar path are tested.
   983	- Response-time and delivery-capacity claims are operationally approved.
