280:## Google Search creative brief
282:### Objective
284:Improve message match within the existing Consulting Search campaign while preserving clear separation from Physiotherapy, ErgoEquip and consumer intent.
288:### Ad-group themes
292:3. Certificate / Course — Mixed Intent (`GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3`), Search-only, Exact/Phrase and gated.
293:4. Manual Handling — Online Delivery (`GOOGLE_CONV_Online-Teams_AU_2026Q3`), Search-only.
296:7. Ergonomic Assessments, with Core informational intent separated from Geo and Remote groups.
303:### RSA construction rules
317:- Refresh or formally reassess Search creative every **8–12 weeks**.
320:### RSA angle library
322:#### Manual Handling Training
339:**Online-delivery note:** use “Manual Handling Online” only for Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Online-Teams_AU_2026Q3`, with organisational framing in a description such as “Flexible online manual-handling training formats for workplace teams.” The verified three-keyword set represents approximately 290 searches/month and the live account also contains a converting online-intent tail. Keep this angle in Search—never port it to Meta, and do not use individual credential language.
349:#### Care-sector manual handling
351:This themed RSA set serves Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Care-Sector_AU_2026Q3`. **Do not build or publish it until sector scope is confirmed, the live aged-care/disability/healthcare negatives are reconciled, and onsite/remote geography is approved; replace `_AU_` with the approved geo if national service is unverified.** It must qualify an organisational buyer and use care-sector workplace language; it must not imply that the viewer or any individual has a disability, injury or health condition.
357:- Healthcare Team Training
366:- Plan practical manual-handling training for care-sector teams and supervisors.
368:- Request a defined training scope for aged-care, healthcare or support teams.
370:#### Certificate / course mixed intent — gated Search-only brief
372:This RSA set serves Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3` and the approximately 3,400-searches-per-month certificate/course pool. Buyer type is **UNCLASSIFIED**. Use Exact and Phrase only, qualify the organisational need in ad copy, and route to the gated certificate LP block. **Do not build or publish until ErgoWorks confirms whether it issues an accredited certificate, statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records and signs off the corresponding claims.** Exclude this theme from Meta.
384:- Ask what training scope and participant records are available for your organisation—only after client sign-off.
387:#### Workplace ergonomic assessment
400:- Australia-Wide Support — **client sign-off required (see geography launch blocker)**
408:#### Implementation and ErgoAssess
427:### Asset themes
451:Any asset referring to awards, client names, customer logos, Danone, “ASX 100,” review ratings or quantified outcomes is **client sign-off required**.
453:### Google Snapshot asset
457:- Free 15-Min Risk Snapshot
460:- B2B Ergonomics Snapshot
470:If the platform format cannot display that caveat clearly and adjacent to the offer within the ad, do not mention or describe the Snapshot in that ad. A destination-page caveat does not cure an unqualified ad placement.
474:## Meta demand-generation creative brief
476:### Objective
480:Meta should not be optimised around cheap raw leads. The intended conversion is a qualified B2B enquiry or Snapshot request, supported by a clean measurement baseline and offline qualification feedback.
482:### Policy-safe messaging rules
484:All Meta messaging must:
492:- Use separate enquiry consent and optional marketing consent.
493:- Pass AU privacy review before pixel, CAPI, CRM or campaign activation.
494:- **The only permitted occurrence of "certificate" or "certification" in Meta creative is inside the mandatory Snapshot caveat: “Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.”** That sanctioned negative caveat is required wherever the Snapshot appears and is not a violation of this rule. Never use certificate/certification as a hook, offer, audience signal or benefit, including when referencing client-sign-off-gated participant attendance or training-completion records. This avoids attracting individual certificate-seeker intent that contaminates a corporate-buyer prospecting audience ("manual handling certificate" drew A$364.86 / 55 clicks in 30 days). This is a positioning and contamination rule, not a claimed Meta review trigger.
496:### Launch creative architecture
498:Use at least **five genuinely distinct creatives per ad set** across at least **three formats**. The starting mix should include:
506:Minor colour or headline variations do not constitute distinct concepts. Meta’s retrieval system may suppress near-identical ads; concepts must differ in angle, visual story and value proposition.
508:### Concept 1 — Start with the task
510:**Audience signal:** WHS, operations, training and workplace decision-makers. Launch targeting: **approved service geography only** (see Appendix B audience strategy). Australia-wide, Canberra/ACT, Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane expansion is wholly behind geography sign-off. Meta has no job-title targeting, so individual credential-seekers must be filtered via negative signals: exclude engagement with personal-credential, generic-course, individual-online-training and TAFE/RTO-style creative CTAs from prospecting, and add an Advantage+ audience exclusion list built from website visitors who bounce off non-B2B pages.
516:*(Tightened toward real query language: "manual handling training" is the best-performing MH term — A$206.89 / 22 clicks / 3 conv — so keeping the exact keyword in the hook preserves message-match relevance without introducing individual-credential language.)*
531:**Baseline CTA:** Request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot. **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
533:### Concept 2 — Three questions leaders need answered
551:**Baseline CTA:** Request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot. **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
553:### Concept 3 — Hybrid consistency
569:**Baseline CTA:** Request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot. **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
571:### Concept 4 — Fitout decisions
587:**Baseline CTA:** Request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot. **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
589:### Concept 5 — Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot
597:> If your team is reviewing its workplace ergonomics priorities — a workstation assessment, a manual-task programme — request a free 15-minute B2B Snapshot and receive a written three-point summary. **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
599:*(Language tightened to the concrete nouns real queries use — "workstation assessment", "manual handling training", "ergonomics assessment" — rather than abstract "one workplace issue" phrasing, to lift relevance without altering the mandatory caveat placement.)*
607:**CTA:** Request the free Snapshot.
609:The caveat must appear within every version of the Snapshot creative or its immediately visible copy block.
611:### Concept 6 — From one-off activity to programme visibility
627:**Baseline CTA:** Request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot. **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
629:Any software screenshot, customer result or implementation metric requires validation. Client logos, Danone, “ASX 100,” awards and the 5.0/63-review claim are **client sign-off required**.
631:### Gated post-baseline service-led CTA tests
633:Only after the Snapshot baseline has sufficient clean volume and qualified-lead evidence may service-led primary CTAs be tested against it. Preserve each concept's organisational framing and use the applicable service CTA: Concept 1, “Request a manual-task programme scope”; Concept 2, “Explore the ErgoWorks implementation pathway”; Concept 3, “Request a hybrid-work programme scope”; Concept 4, “Discuss a workplace or fitout review”; Concept 6, “Explore ongoing programme management.” These are post-baseline test variants, not launch creative, and must not be presented as simultaneous competing CTAs within a Snapshot execution.
635:### Meta copy limits and production specifications
638:- Keep primary text below **125 characters** where the required Snapshot caveat is not involved.
639:- Snapshot caveats take precedence over brevity.
644:- Keep essential Reels content away from the bottom 35%, where interface elements may obscure it.
650:- Test Advantage+ Creative enhancements through controlled splits; do not assume automatic variations preserve regulated wording or caveats.
652:### Refresh and fatigue rules
654:- Review Meta creative every **14–21 days**.
655:- Refresh or broaden the concept pool if prospecting frequency exceeds **5.0**.
656:- Refresh or reassess audience size if retargeting frequency exceeds **12.0**.
657:- Treat a CTR decline greater than **20% over 14 days** as a creative-fatigue failure.
665:## Dedicated landing-page message brief
667:### Page role
675:Manual Handling Training should be the first variant because it is the **2,700-searches-per-month Australian demand head** and currently represents **49% of Consulting Search spend in the last 30 days**.
677:Within that first variant, prepare the explicitly gated, scope-pending modules in Appendix A: care-sector for Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Care-Sector_AU_2026Q3`; flexible online-team delivery for `GOOGLE_CONV_Online-Teams_AU_2026Q3`; and refresher/recurring programme for `GOOGLE_CONV_Refresher-Teams_AU_2026Q3`. **None may publish until the client confirms the service, delivery format and approved geography.** The care module also requires reconciliation of the live aged-care/disability/healthcare negatives. The online module is Search-only and must never be used as a Meta angle. Refresher cadence, participant outputs and recurring-service framing remain client-sign-off-dependent.
679:### Core structure
685:5. Verified proof.
687:7. Compliant Snapshot offer block with the adjacent “preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis” caveat.
689:9. Privacy and consent controls.
692:### Hero directions
694:**Launch default:** the Snapshot is the single dominant CTA on every baseline variant. Every placement that offers or describes it must carry adjacent wording that it is preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis. If the format cannot carry that caveat, the format must not mention the Snapshot.
696:#### Manual Handling Training
703:> **Request a free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot**  
706:#### Workstation and ergonomic assessment
711:Primary CTA: **Request a free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot.** **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
713:#### Hybrid programme
718:Primary CTA: **Request a free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot.** **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
720:### Post-baseline service-plan-primary tests
722:The service-plan-primary variants—**Request a Training Plan**, **Request an Assessment Plan** and **Request a Hybrid Programme Scope**—are not launch defaults. Test them only after each matching Snapshot-primary baseline has at least 30 valid lead-entry conversions and two complete conversion-lag cycles. Allocate traffic 50/50 within one intent-matched variant, change only the CTA hierarchy, and run for at least 14 days unless a compliance or tracking failure requires an earlier stop. Adopt a service-plan-primary variant only if it improves CRM-qualified-lead rate with no more than a 20% deterioration in cost per qualified lead; otherwise retain the Snapshot-primary baseline. Snapshot booked/held remain CRM stages, not platform events.
724:### Form requirements
744:- Pain or symptom information.
746:- Workers-compensation case information.
751:- Optional consent to receive future marketing.
753:The page, CMP, **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, Meta Pixel/CAPI plan, GA4 stream and GTM scope require AU privacy review before launch. Consulting data must remain isolated from Physiotherapy, ErgoEquip and Biosymm.
757:## Future LinkedIn ABM brief
759:LinkedIn is a later test, not an initial dependency. It should be considered only when contract value, target-account quality, sales capacity and budget justify the platform’s higher cost.
761:### Potential audiences
770:### Recommended concepts
778:If LinkedIn launches:
780:- Allocate at least 30% of its test budget to Thought Leader Ads.
781:- Test at least two formats.
785:- Avoid unverified proof and personal-health implications.
786:- Obtain **client sign-off required** before using any customer name, logo, testimonial, award, “ASX 100” claim, Danone reference or review claim.
790:## Proof framework and approval status
800:| Danone name or testimonial | ErgoScale/ErgoControl proof | **Client sign-off required** |
801:| “ASX 100” claim | Enterprise scale proof | **Client sign-off required** |
802:| 5.0 rating / 63 reviews | General trust proof | **Client sign-off required** |
809:## Creative production priorities
814:| 2 | Dedicated landing-page modules and compliant Snapshot blocks | Replace generic-page message mismatch |
815:| 3 | Five genuinely distinct Meta concepts across static, video and carousel | Establish demand-generation coverage |
816:| 4 | Snapshot consultant video, static and carousel | Test the low-friction B2B entry offer |
820:| 8 | Future LinkedIn document and Thought Leader assets | Enable a gated ABM pilot |
826:## Compliance and pre-launch approval checklist
830:| Claims | No guarantee of injury prevention, WHS compliance, claim reduction or quantified financial outcome |
831:| Snapshot | Every description states that it is B2B-only, covers one issue, includes a written three-point summary, and carries: **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.** |
832:| Meta policy | No personal-condition implications or health-status targeting |
834:| Consent | Enquiry consent separated from optional marketing consent |
835:| Privacy | AU privacy review completed before launch |
836:| Tracking | CMP plus **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent** configured before activation |
839:| Proof | Every customer logo, award, Danone reference, “ASX 100” claim and 5.0/63-review claim receives client sign-off |
841:| Creative QA | Copy, crop, captions, safe zones, CTA and landing-page message match checked on mobile |
846:## Not assessed / data required before implementation
850:| Current Search creative | Current RSAs, assets, pinning and Ad Strength are absent from the snapshot | Export all active ads and assets by ad group |
851:| Search intent | 30-day search terms, full keyword/match-type inventory and negatives were pulled 2026-07-12 (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`, `research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`) | Remaining: 90-day query history before final restructuring |
852:| Search diagnostics | Keyword-level Quality Scores pulled 2026-07-12; component diagnostics (expected CTR, ad relevance, LP experience) still absent | Export keyword-level Quality Score components |
853:| Individual vs organisational search-intent split | Not quantified: the 55 clicks / 1.67 conversions on "manual handling certificate" are unclassified in current Search conversion data and could be inflating the "20 real leads/month" estimate used to derive the A$84.92 Meta CPA planning anchor | Classify certificate-term conversions before treating the anchor as corporate-lead economics |
854:| Meta lookalike seed purity | Certificate-intent clicks exist in the funnel; the "qualified leads" lookalike seed has no defined filter step | Audit whether any future seed pool contains individual/job-seeker enquiries misfiled as corporate leads by CRM stage, before enabling lookalikes |
855:| Search settings | Geo, device, schedule, network and audience settings are absent | Campaign-settings audit before finalising variants |
856:| Creative performance | No asset-level CTR, CVR or time-series creative data | Establish baseline by ad, asset, placement and audience |
857:| Fatigue | No 14-day CTR trend or Meta frequency exists; Meta is currently greenfield | Assess only after sufficient live delivery; apply the defined thresholds |
858:| Meta account | Pixel, CAPI, Business Manager, audience and creative inventory status not supplied | Technical and privacy audit before build |
859:| Snapshot operations | Consultant capacity, eligibility, turnaround, booking flow and service geography are unconfirmed | Client approval of service-level rules |
861:| Proof | Awards, Danone, “ASX 100,” 5.0/63 reviews, logos and rollout claims are unverified | Documentary evidence and client sign-off |
866:| Consent and privacy | CMP, **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, privacy notices and cross-business data boundaries not assessed | Australian privacy review and documented implementation scope |
868:| Creative decisions | No clean baseline supports kill or scale directives | Use conditional diagnosis after qualified-lead data exists |
869:| LinkedIn ABM | Named-account list, deal economics and minimum viable test budget are unknown | Validate account universe, economics and sales follow-up capacity |

