    60	- 4 Newsletter Sign Ups counted as Primary
    61	- 1 Email Click
    62	- 1 Call Forwarding
    63	
    64	This means reported conversion volume overstates genuine leads and currently gives Maximize Conversions an impure optimisation signal. There is no qualified-lead or closed-won import.
    65	
    66	### Search concentration
    67	
    68	Manual Handling Training received **A$2,069—49% of the A$4,246 last-30-day spend**. Manual handling training remains the current spend anchor and largest verified **TRAINING** term at **2,700 Australian searches per month**; research also identifies an approximately **3,400-searches-per-month mixed-intent certificate/course pool** with buyer type **UNCLASSIFIED** and an approximately **780-searches-per-month care-sector opportunity**. These are directional demand estimates, not forecasts or verified service fit, and both expansion pockets remain gated as set out in Appendices A–D.
    69	
    70	Other notable last-30-day results include:
    71	
    72	| Ad group | Spend | Reported conversions | Interpretation |
    73	|---|---:|---:|---|
    74	| Manual Handling Training | A$2,069 | 10.5 | Dominant demand, but query and lead quality are unverified |
    75	| “DSA — Ergoworks Consulting” | A$795 | 4.5 | Not DSA: nine static EXACT terms form a competitor/generic group; total quality is unverified, while only the sampled government/competitor-query subset was near-zero converting |
    76	| Ergonomic Office Consulting | A$719 | 7 | Reported CPA approximately A$103; validate conversion quality before expansion |
    77	| Ergonomics Assessments | A$531 | 3 | Diagnose after conversion cleanup |
    78	| Workplace Ergonomics | A$133 | 1 | Insufficient evidence for a directional decision |
    79	| Brand | A$0 | 0 | All three dedicated Brand terms are paused; the same three terms are duplicated across five service groups, so repair requires in-place re-enablement and de-duplication before any breakout decision |
    80	
    81	Paid traffic currently lands on generic WordPress pages, led by the Manual Handling Training page with 234 clicks in the last 30 days. There is no dedicated paid-media conversion page.
    82	
    83	### Scope limitation
    84	
    85	The available evidence includes last-30-day search terms, the full keyword inventory with match types, statuses and headline Quality Scores, 493 negatives and a partial geography signal. Remaining gaps are longer search-term and keyword-performance history, the negative-list audit, RSAs/assets, complete campaign settings, Quality Score components and geo/device performance reports. Consequently, the package supports a diagnostic plan—not unconditional pause, restructure or scale instructions.
   250	- Retain Maximize Conversions while the clean baseline forms.
   251	- Launch one consolidated Meta website-lead prospecting ad set under Scenario 1 or 2.
   252	- Fund Meta at no less than A$20/day.
   253	- Use at least three materially distinct formats and five approved creatives.
   254	- Optimise initially to valid Snapshot requests; each Snapshot placement must state: **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
   255	- Validate click-ID, UTM, CRM-stage, Pixel/CAPI and deduplication flows.
   256	- Build Consulting-only retargeting audiences without activating a separately underfunded ad set.
   257	- Review search terms weekly and classify any product or Physiotherapy bleed.
   258	
   259	**Committed leading indicators:** approved destination coverage; minimum Meta delivery floor; delivery, CTR, form-start and Snapshot-request baselines; identifiers retained; no known cross-business bleed left unclassified.
   260	
   261	### Days 61–90 — Diagnose and decide
   262	
   263	- Assign each Search cluster a status: retain, repair, insufficient data or candidate test.
   264	- Compare Meta concepts and formats without fragmenting the budget.
   265	- Replace the provisional Meta CPA assumption with observed Snapshot-request data.
   266	- Reconcile raw leads to CRM-qualified leads and proposals.
   267	- Complete the commercial target-CPA worksheet or mark it not assessable.
   268	- Issue a written PMax fund-to-floor or park decision.
   269	- Issue a separate paid-remarketing rebuild or park decision.
   270	- Propose any budget increase in increments no greater than 20%, followed by 3–5 days of observation and conversion-lag review.
   271	
   272	No segment receives an unconditional kill or scale label during the first 90 days. The 3× Kill Rule requires an approved clean target CPA, and the methodology’s full scaling threshold of at least 50 conversions per week is far above the current approximately 20 real leads per month.
   273	
   274	Any 12-month lead, CPA or revenue trajectory remains an assumption-labelled scenario—not a commitment.
   275	
   276	## 9. Risks and compliance gates
   277	
   278	| Gate | Requirement | Launch consequence |
   279	|---|---|---|
   280	| Claims | No guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance, quantified claims reduction or guaranteed financial outcome | Blocks affected creative or page copy |
   281	| Snapshot description | Every placement must state: preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis | Blocks affected ad, form or page |
   282	| OAIC APP 3 | No injury, symptom, diagnosis, treatment, claim or other health fields in advertising forms | Blocks form launch |
   283	| Meta personal attributes | Use workplace- and role-level language; never imply that the viewer or their team has a health condition | Blocks affected Meta creative |
   284	| Consent | Required enquiry consent must be separate from optional, unchecked marketing consent | Blocks form launch |
   285	| Privacy | Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent. CMP, pixel/CAPI field mapping, call tracking and CRM uploads require Australian privacy/legal approval | Blocks all new paid-social, LP tracking, remarketing and offline activation |
   286	| Sensitive data | No free-text enquiry content, medical data, call content or Physiotherapy data may be sent to advertising platforms—even hashed | Blocks measurement activation |
   287	| Proof | Awards, “ASX 100,” 5.0/63 reviews, client logos and Danone references are **client sign-off required** wherever proposed | Blocks those proof assets |
   288	| Isolation | Campaign-level controls and Consulting-specific measurement scope must prevent ErgoEquip, Biosymm and Physiotherapy contamination | Blocks affected campaign or dataset |
   289	| PMax | Clean goals, offline loop, dedicated LP, verified assets, URL controls, exclusions and A$50/day funding | Otherwise remains parked |
   290	| Remarketing | Privacy approval, sufficient isolated audiences, approved creative, frequency controls and separate viable funding | Otherwise remains parked |

